Create a full HTML and JavaScript (Three.js) implementation that simulates a 3D sneaker viewer based on the following requirements:

Base Scene Setup
- Use `Three.js` to render a 3D sneaker model inside a transparent canvas.
- Set the background of the canvas and the scene to fully transparent.
- Ensure the canvas supports antialiasing.
- Add default lighting to simulate ambient light.
- Enable camera control using orbit-style controls, but restrict the vertical angle to a minimum of -0.01 and a maximum of 0.01 radians.
- Use a PerspectiveCamera positioned at z = 50 units.

3D Model Loading
- Load a USDZ (or alternatively a GLB/GLTF) model of a sneaker. Place it at the center of the scene.
- Once the model is loaded:
  - Automatically scale the model so its maximum dimension is 30 units.
  - Center the model in X, Y, and Z axes.
  - Continuously rotate it on the Y-axis (360 degrees every 6 seconds).

Texturing & Coloring
- The sneaker must support dynamic color changes using different textures for accent colors.
- Use 5 layers of PNG textures:
  - `texture_sneaker_1.png`
  - `texture_sneaker_2.png`
  - `texture_sneaker_3.png`
  - `texture_sneaker_4.png`
  - `texture_sneaker_5.png`
- Apply color tints dynamically to each of these layers using a selected "GearColor" object.
- Composite the final sneaker texture on a canvas of 1024x1024 px, then apply it as a material to the mesh node named `"Plane_2"` (or similar).

Camera Effects
- Add camera post-processing effects such as:
  - Bloom effect (intensity: 0.7, blur radius: 5)
  - Motion blur (intensity: 0.5)
  - Contrast: 0.5
  - Saturation: 1.05
  - Focal length: 40
- Disable automatic exposure adaptation.

Logic & Visibility Handling
- Only load and display the 3D sneaker if it is visible in the viewport.
- Add a cleanup routine that pauses animations and removes the model from the scene when it's off-screen or the view is destroyed.

Animation
- Add an infinite Y-axis rotation animation to the entire model with a duration of 6 seconds per full rotation.
- Ensure the animation is time-based and synced with scene rendering time (not CSS).

Interactivity
- Use mouse/touch interaction to orbit the camera around the sneaker.
- Do **not** allow zooming or panning—only restricted orbit rotation.

Optional Debug Tools
- Add an option to enable bounding boxes and world origin visualization for debugging purposes.

Assets Needed
- A GLTF or USDZ 3D model named `sneaker_model.glb` or similar.
- 5 PNG textures: `texture_sneaker_1.png` to `texture_sneaker_5.png`.

Color Configuration
- Define a `GearColor` object with:
  - `mainColor`, `accent1`, `accent2`, `accent3`, `accent4`
- Use this to tint each corresponding texture layer when compositing the final texture dynamically.

Deployment Considerations
- Ensure the viewer works smoothly on mobile and desktop.
- Use responsive sizing for the canvas container.

Name the main HTML file: `index.html` and keep all assets in a folder `/assets`.
